SUMMARY OF TERMS & CONDITIONS:
------------------------------

1. TURNKEY SALE & FULL SOURCE CODE TRANSFER
The Developer delivers the complete, uncompiled source code (backend, relational 
database schemas, frontend modules, integrations, documentation) to the Client. 
This is a one-time turnkey purchase with zero recurring software seat fees, zero 
cloud lock-in, and zero remote disabling mechanisms.

2. RIGHTS CONFERRED TO THE CLIENT
The Developer grants to the Client an exclusive-in-business, perpetual, irrevocable, 
worldwide, royalty-free right to:
(a) Self-host, deploy, and execute the Software on any server or private infrastructure 
    for all internal business and logistics operations;
(b) Freely modify, adapt, configure, maintain, and expand the source code internally 
    or via third-party developers;
(c) The Client shall NOT resell, sublicense, rent, or distribute the Software as an 
    independent off-the-shelf commercial SaaS offering to external third parties.

3. PATERNITY & ATTRIBUTION (WATERMARK PRESERVATION)
Under Article 9 of Moroccan Copyright Law (Loi n° 2-00), moral rights of paternity 
are inalienable and perpetual:
(a) The Client explicitly acknowledges Salaheddine CHIKHI / AVYR Digital as the 
    sole original author and system architect of the Software.
(b) The Client agrees to permanently preserve the visible watermark 
    "Powered by AVYR Digital" / "Engineered by AVYR Digital (Salaheddine CHIKHI)" 
    within software navigation headers, portal interfaces, login screen, 
    system footers, HTTP response headers, and source code comments.
(c) Removing, masking, or obscuring author credits without express written consent 
    is strictly prohibited.

4. BACKGROUND IP & DEVELOPER REUSE RIGHTS (TRONC COMMUN)
The Client owns all custom proprietary business rules and specific brand data. 
However, all underlying framework architectures, generic database schema designs, 
authentication systems, inventory deduction algorithms, and technical libraries 
("Background IP") remain the intellectual property of AVYR Digital.
AVYR Digital explicitly retains the unrestricted right to reuse, adapt, and deploy 
these core components and know-how for other past, present, or future clients and projects.

5. NON-COMPETE ON CUSTOM CONFIGURATION
The Developer agrees not to deliver the Client's exact tailored operational configuration 
or proprietary custom business logic to any direct commercial competitor of the Client 
in the Client's specific retail market niche in Morocco for a period of 12 months.

6. GOVERNING LAW & JURISDICTION
This Agreement is governed by the laws of the Kingdom of Morocco. Any dispute that 
cannot be resolved amicably shall be submitted to the exclusive jurisdiction of the 
Commercial Court of Casablanca (Tribunal de Commerce de Casablanca, Maroc).

